<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela TEMs should not set interest rates - Casas.</title>
<headline>Venezuela TEMs should not set interest rates - Casas.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Venezuelan Central Bank's weekly issues of monetary stabilization, or TEM, bills should not continue to be the benchmark by which Venezuela's interest rates are set, central Bank President Antonio Casas Gonzalez said Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;We have to change this...The market indicator has to be something else,&quot; Casas said during a hearing of the Senate Finance Committee.</p>
<p>Casas said the Central Bank's discount rate would be a better benchmark for interest rates.</p>
<p>-- Paul Hughes, Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600</p>
</text>
